# ==========================================================
# FROZEN SCIENTIFIC ARTIFACTS — BYTE IDENTITY IS THE GUARANTEE
# ==========================================================
# M7_PREREGISTRATION.md is frozen and its identity is defined by a SHA-256
# over its exact bytes (see M7_PREREGISTRATION.sha256:
# 2f12e309d7409e95f3d1bca34135110e518865fd01d96e5eeaee347b6e33f6b9,
# 55124 bytes, 874 lines). The stored blob reproduces that digest exactly.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE the digest does not survive a checkout. On Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites LF to CRLF on the way out, and the working
# copy hashes to 953d6910a287667fee7969f4a7de909bb5051667100bafacb037837ead154771
# instead. Anyone validating the frozen artifact against their working copy
# would get a mismatch and correctly conclude it had been tampered with.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in BOTH directions for these paths,
# so checkout content is byte-identical to the committed blob on every
# platform. This modifies no frozen document, threshold, seed range,
# acceptance criterion or evidence — it only stops git from rewriting bytes
# whose exactness is the whole integrity claim.
#
# The errata are covered for the same reason: each binds to the frozen digest
# and they form a cumulative chain (ERR-09 cites ERR-01..ERR-08), so the
# supersession record must be reproducible with the same fidelity.

research/cognitive-audit/M7_PREREGISTRATION.md          -text
research/cognitive-audit/M7_PREREGISTRATION.sha256      -text
research/cognitive-audit/M7_PREREGISTRATION_ERRATUM_*.md -text

# M8 pre-registration — same byte-integrity guarantee as the M7 frozen artifact.
# Its identity is a SHA-256 over exact bytes (M8_PREREGISTRATION.sha256), so end-of-line
# conversion must be disabled in both directions or the digest fails to validate on checkout.
research/preregistrations/M8_PREREGISTRATION.md      -text
research/preregistrations/M8_PREREGISTRATION.sha256  -text
